WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.588
This slide shows why CMDB
hygiene isn't a nicety.

2
00:00:03.588 --> 00:00:07.094
A missing, duplicate or stale
record breaks patching and

3
00:00:07.094 --> 00:00:10.824
evidence in different ways, and
the table walks through each.

4
00:00:10.824 --> 00:00:13.827
Duplicates come from
the sources themselves,

5
00:00:13.827 --> 00:00:16.513
from reimaged devices to merged records.

6
00:00:16.513 --> 00:00:20.530
The rule is to bind, not delete:
keep the record that carries the

7
00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:25.100
authoritative identity, and move
its tickets and findings over first.

8
00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:29.577
Stale records follow a sequence:
detect, have the owner confirm,

9
00:00:29.577 --> 00:00:34.313
retire, and only then delete, because
some deletions can't be undone.

10
00:00:34.313 --> 00:00:39.137
A deleted device, for example, takes
its BitLocker recovery keys with it.

11
00:00:39.137 --> 00:00:41.001
That closes Module 3.

12
00:00:41.001 --> 00:00:43.940
Module 4 turns to control automation.
